  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nStacked surface and upper low will drift from southern \nSaskatchewan to Manitoba tonight. The strongest winds will subside\nand the High Wind Warning expiring at midnight looks good. A\nBlowing Dust Advisory is in effect until 6 pm and this also looks\nlike a good ending point.\n\nFriday, the winds will increase a bit but not be as strong as\ntoday. The surface low will drift into western Ontario while a\nslow moving cold front drops south close to the Montana/Canada\nborder.\n\nAn upper trough will move into Montana on Sunday allowing an\nincrease in lift and possibly rain for the area. The models are\nshowing the upper low to dig into the central Rockies Monday that\nwill push the precipitation shield to our south but the CWA may be\nlucky enough to be on the northern edge of it. Some of the models\nare showing it to be cold enough for snow. Weather grids right now\nspelling out for just Sunday night. Will have to keep an eye out\nfor this one if the models bring this system further north, there\ncould be significant impacts.\n\nThe upper trough begins to lift out Tuesday so a return to more\nnormal conditions can be expected for the remainder of the seven\ndays.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nA blend with the GLAMP in wind grids were made. No other\ndeviations were made. TFJ",
